  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Suppose $m$ and $n$ are both odd. Prove that $m^2-n^2$ is divisible by 4.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Write $m=2j+1$ and $n=2k+1$, where $j,k$ are integers. Then $m^2-n^2=4(j-k)(j+k+1)$, so it is divisible by 4.",
      "worked": "Write $m=2j+1$ and $n=2k+1$, where $j,k$ are integers.\n$$\\begin{align*}m^2-n^2&=(m-n)(m+n)\\\\m^2-n^2&=((2j+1)-(2k+1))((2j+1)+(2k+1))\\\\m^2-n^2&=(2j-2k)(2j+2k+2)\\\\m^2-n^2&=4(j-k)(j+k+1).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(j-k)(j+k+1)$ is an integer, $m^2-n^2$ is divisible by 4.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
